From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:35:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] Skip GLM FP8 attn-proj dequant when the target is
 quantized

Source: knapcio/GLM-5.3-Flash-4x-DGX-Spark-TP4, overlay/qmix_patch.py
(the _try_load_fp8_attn_proj dtype guard), commit 770d115, MIT License,
author knapcio. Logic re-implemented, not copied verbatim.

Upstream status: not upstream. vLLM main (0f112d180) still dequantizes
whenever no `weight_scale_inv` param exists.

What/why: _try_load_fp8_attn_proj matches any `.q_a_proj.`,
`.kv_a_proj_with_mqa.`, `.q_b_proj.` or `.o_proj.` FP8 weight or scale
tensor, including ModelOpt's `weight_scale` name. It dequantizes to BF16
unless a `weight_scale_inv` param exists. A ModelOpt FP8_PB_WO or MXFP8
projection stores its scale as `weight_scale` with an FP8 weight param,
so the helper would block-dequantize it into an FP8 param and corrupt
it. The `.o_proj.` suffix also catches KDA o_proj. Dequantize only when
the target param is BF16/FP16/FP32; otherwise the normal loader handles
the quantized tensors. No change for BF16 targets (the FP8 Z.ai release).

Claimed gain and config: none on its own. It is a prerequisite for the
lossless8 checkpoint (tools/lossless8.py). knapcio README (2026-09-28)
reports lossless8 at step -7.5 ms with 0.25% output error on 4x DGX Spark
TP=4, served W8A16 via Marlin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py
index 7beec5667..d5274cc7b 100644
--- a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py
@@ -1329,6 +1329,16 @@ def _try_load_fp8_attn_proj(
     # handle it (it has a weight_scale_inv param).
     if target_s in params_dict:
         return False
+    # Likewise when the target was created quantized under another scale name
+    # (ModelOpt FP8_PB_WO / MXFP8 ``weight_scale``, which also reaches KDA
+    # o_proj via the ``.o_proj.`` suffix): only BF16 targets are dequantized.
+    target = params_dict.get(target_w)
+    if target is not None and target.dtype not in (
+        torch.bfloat16,
+        torch.float16,
+        torch.float32,
+    ):
+        return False
 
     entry = buf.setdefault(layer_prefix, {}).setdefault(key, {})
     entry["weight" if is_weight else "scale"] = tensor
